# Create repository sessions

`--create-repo` should modify `--create` and `--switch` to initialize a fresh
colocated repository before creating its tmux session.

    :bins jj tmux cat sh sed mkdir

> [!NOTE]
> 'jj', 'tmux', 'cat', 'sh', 'sed', and 'mkdir' are available.

    :copy tests/fixtures/jjconfig.toml .jjconfig.toml (copied)

    :w smth.toml (written)
```toml
[repo]
root = "config-repos"

[tmux]
setup = "tmux set-option @smth.test-created yes"
```

    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)

The modifier takes no argument: `--create` supplies the directory name, preserved
exactly while the tmux name is sanitized. It
should initialize below the configured root and create a detached session with
repository metadata and the usual setup script.

    :$ smth --config smth.toml --no-base --create-repo --create "project one" (exit: 0)

```stdout
project-one
```

    :$ sh -c 'test -d "config-repos/project one/.jj" && test -d "config-repos/project one/.git"' (exit: 0)

    :t show-options -qv -t '=project-one:' @smth.test-created (success)

```
yes
```

    :$ sh -c 'tmux show-options -qv -t "=project-one:" @smth.repo | sed "s#$PWD#<ROOT>#g"' (exit: 0)

```stdout
<ROOT>/config-repos/project one
```

    :$ sh -c 'tmux display-message -p -t "=project-one:0.0" "#{pane_current_path}" | sed "s#$PWD#<ROOT>#g"' (exit: 0)

```stdout
<ROOT>/config-repos/project one
```

    :t display-message -p '#{client_session}' (success)

```
runner
```

Repeating the request should fail without choosing another directory. The
modifier can also follow the action's name.

    :$ sh -c 'smth --config smth.toml --no-base --create "project one" --create-repo 2> error; status=$?; sed "s#$PWD#<ROOT>#g" error >&2; exit "$status"' (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: repo '<ROOT>/config-repos/project one' already exists
```

    :$ sh -c 'test ! -e "config-repos/project one~1" && test -d "config-repos/project one/.jj"' (exit: 0)

Dots are preserved in the path even when the sanitized tmux name collides.

    :t new-session -d -s foo-bar "cat" (success)
    :t new-session -d -s foo-bar~1 "cat" (success)
    :$ smth --config smth.toml --no-base --create foo.bar --create-repo (exit: 0)

```stdout
foo-bar~2
```

    :$ sh -c 'test -d config-repos/foo.bar/.jj && test ! -e config-repos/foo.bar~2' (exit: 0)

    :$ sh -c 'tmux show-options -qv -t "=foo-bar~2:" @smth.repo | sed "s#$PWD#<ROOT>#g"' (exit: 0)

```stdout
<ROOT>/config-repos/foo.bar
```

Configuring a repository root must not change the existing plain-session
behavior.

    :$ smth --config smth.toml --no-base --create bare (exit: 0)

```stdout
bare
```

    :t show-options -qv -t '=bare:' @smth.repo (success)

    :$ sh -c 'test ! -e config-repos/bare' (exit: 0)

Adding `--create-repo` must disambiguate instead of reusing or converting the
plain session.

    :$ smth --config smth.toml --no-base --create bare --create-repo (exit: 0)

```stdout
bare~1
```

    :$ sh -c 'test -d config-repos/bare/.jj && test ! -e config-repos/bare~1' (exit: 0)

    :t show-options -qv -t '=bare:' @smth.repo (success)

A command-line root should override the configured root.

    :$ smth --config smth.toml --no-base --repo-root cli-repos --create override --create-repo (exit: 0)

```stdout
override
```

    :$ sh -c 'test -d cli-repos/override/.jj && test ! -e config-repos/override' (exit: 0)

An occupied path should be rejected without modifying the existing directory.

    :$ mkdir config-repos/collision (exit: 0)

    :t new-session -d -s collision~1 "cat" (success)

    :$ sh -c 'smth --config smth.toml --no-base --create collision --create-repo 2> error; status=$?; sed "s#$PWD#<ROOT>#g" error >&2; exit "$status"' (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: repo '<ROOT>/config-repos/collision' already exists
```

    :$ sh -c 'test ! -e config-repos/collision~2 && test ! -e config-repos/collision/.jj' (exit: 0)

`--switch` with the modifier should perform the same initialization and name
disambiguation before switching the client, leaving the existing session alone.
Its stdout should report the disambiguated name, not the requested one.

    :t new-session -d -s switched "cat" (success)
    :t respawn-pane -k -t runner:0.0 'smth --config smth.toml --no-base --repo-root switch-repos --switch switched --create-repo > switch-name; tmux wait-for -S switched-repo; cat' (success)
    :t wait-for switched-repo (success)
    :$ cat switch-name (exit: 0)

```stdout
switched~1
```

    :t display-message -p '#{client_session}' (success)

```
switched~1
```

    :$ sh -c 'test -d switch-repos/switched/.jj && test -d switch-repos/switched/.git' (exit: 0)

    :t has-session -t '=switched' (success)
    :t switch-client -t runner (success)
    :pane runner:0.0

Without either root setting, creation should default to the process working
directory.

    :w no-root.toml (written)
```toml
[repo]
globs = []
```

    :$ mkdir fallback (exit: 0)

    :$ sh -c 'cd fallback && smth --config ../no-root.toml --no-base --create local --create-repo' (exit: 0)

```stdout
local
```

    :$ sh -c 'test -d fallback/local/.jj && test -d fallback/local/.git' (exit: 0)

Names that sanitize to empty should use numeric suffixes, including when the
repository root does not exist yet. The root itself must not be initialized.

    :$ smth --config smth.toml --no-base --repo-root unnamed-repos --create ... --create-repo (exit: 0)

```stdout
1
```

    :$ sh -c 'test -d unnamed-repos/.../.jj && test -d unnamed-repos/.../.git && test ! -e unnamed-repos/.jj' (exit: 0)

Empty, omitted, and invalid directory names should be rejected.

    :$ smth --config smth.toml --no-base --create "" --create-repo (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: repo names must be non-empty
```

    :$ smth --config smth.toml --no-base --create --create-repo (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: a repository name is required
```

    :$ smth --config smth.toml --no-base --switch --create-repo (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: a repository name is required
```

    :$ smth --config smth.toml --no-base --create ../escape --create-repo (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: repo names must not be '.' or '..'
```

    :$ smth --config smth.toml --no-base --create /absolute --create-repo (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: repo names must not be absolute paths
```

    :$ smth --config smth.toml --no-base --create . --create-repo (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: repo names must not be '.' or '..'
```

    :$ smth --config smth.toml --no-base --create nested/repo --create-repo (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: repository names must not contain path separators
```

    :$ smth --config smth.toml --no-base --create .. --create-repo (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: repo names must not be '.' or '..'
```

    :$ smth --config smth.toml --no-base --create ./relative --create-repo (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: repo names must not be '.' or '..'
```

Single normal components are accepted with trailing separators. Backslashes are
ordinary filename characters on Unix.

    :$ smth --config smth.toml --no-base --create 'a\b' --create-repo (exit: 0)

```stdout
a-b
```

    :$ sh -c 'test -d "config-repos/a\b/.jj" && test -d "config-repos/a\b/.git"' (exit: 0)

    :$ smth --config smth.toml --no-base --create trailing/ --create-repo (exit: 0)

```stdout
trailing
```

    :$ sh -c 'test -d config-repos/trailing/.jj && test -d config-repos/trailing/.git' (exit: 0)

A trailing `/.` passes component validation, but jj cannot initialize that path.
No repository or tmux session should be created.

    :$ smth --config smth.toml --no-base --create dotted/. --create-repo (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: error running 'jj git init': Error: Failed to create workspace
Caused by: No such file or directory (os error 2)
```

    :$ sh -c 'test ! -e config-repos/dotted/.jj && test ! -e config-repos/dotted/.git' (exit: 0)

    :t has-session -t '=dotted' (failure)

```
can't find session: dotted
```

    :t display-message -p '#{client_session}' (success)

```
runner
```

Repository creation requires an empty context and rejects incompatible or
competing actions.

    :$ sh -c 'cd "config-repos/project one" && smth --config ../../smth.toml --create nested --create-repo' (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: repo creation requires no base
```

    :$ smth --config smth.toml --base "config-repos/project one" --create nested --create-repo (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: repo creation requires no base
```

    :$ smth --config smth.toml --no-base --onto @ --create invalid --create-repo (exit: 2)

```stderr
error: the argument '--onto <REV>' cannot be used with '--create-repo'

Usage: smth --config <PATH> --no-base --onto <REV> --create [<SESSION>]

For more information, try 'help'.
```

    :$ smth --config smth.toml --no-base --create first --switch second --create-repo (exit: 2)

```stderr
error: the argument '--create [<SESSION>]' cannot be used with '--switch [<SESSION>]'

Usage: smth --config <PATH> --no-base --create-repo <--create [<SESSION>]|--switch [<SESSION>]>

For more information, try 'help'.
```

The modifier requires a create or switch action. It takes no operand of its own
and cannot be used with other actions or picker filtering options.

    :$ smth --config smth.toml --no-base --create-repo (exit: 2)

```stderr
error: the following required arguments were not provided:
  <--create [<SESSION>]|--switch [<SESSION>]>

Usage: smth --config <PATH> --no-base --create-repo <--create [<SESSION>]|--switch [<SESSION>]>

For more information, try 'help'.
```

    :$ smth --config smth.toml --no-base --create-repo unexpected --create invalid (exit: 2)

```stderr
error: unrecognized subcommand 'unexpected'

Usage: smth [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

For more information, try 'help'.
```

